Related PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/pull/216

## Node dragging no longer moves graph nodes

At head `147ba5216fef33466344e8ff6f78e9419043ac60`, the graph's mouse and single-touch drag handlers change `fx/fy`, but the rendered `x/y` coordinates never follow them.

- The PR initializes `paused = true`: [graph-canvas.ts:215](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/blob/147ba5216fef33466344e8ff6f78e9419043ac60/public/src/views/graph-canvas.ts#L210-L217)
- [tick():912–915](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/blob/147ba5216fef33466344e8ff6f78e9419043ac60/public/src/views/graph-canvas.ts#L912-L915) returns while paused. Neither `togglePhysics` nor `reheat` now clears that flag
- [beginPointerDrag():1919–1925](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/blob/147ba5216fef33466344e8ff6f78e9419043ac60/public/src/views/graph-canvas.ts#L1919-L1925) cancels any settle worker, while [handleDragMove():1943–1948](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/blob/147ba5216fef33466344e8ff6f78e9419043ac60/public/src/views/graph-canvas.ts#L1943-L1948) changes only `fx/fy`
- [endNodeDrag():1971–1973](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/blob/147ba5216fef33466344e8ff6f78e9419043ac60/public/src/views/graph-canvas.ts#L1971-L1973) then clears those target coordinates without applying them

Independent source-method reproduction used the exact base/head GraphCanvas class methods with a synthetic one-node fixture. Palette, hit-testing and coordinate transforms were stubbed; no browser, live project, server, or Core CLI was used. Starting at (10,20), dragging to (110,120), advancing one frame and releasing gives:

| Source | During drag | After release |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Base `ef7ea8dad901c29af2612d97e5856d1f0671f53d` | (110,120) | (110,120) |
| PR `147ba5216fef33466344e8ff6f78e9419043ac60` | (10,20) | (10,20) |

The following standalone method fixture can also run against each checkout after its normal frontend build. Run it as an ES module from the repository root; `paused` is read from that checkout's actual source initializer:

```js
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
import { GraphCanvas } from './public/src/views/graph-canvas.js';

const source = readFileSync('public/src/views/graph-canvas.ts', 'utf8');
const paused = /private paused = true;/.test(source);
const graph = Object.create(GraphCanvas.prototype);
const node = {
  id: 'fixture', label: 'Fixture', type: 'task',
  status: 'open', lane: 'item', degree: 0,
  x: 10, y: 20, vx: 0, vy: 0, fx: null, fy: null
};
Object.assign(graph, {
  nodes: [node], edges: [], particles: [], lastParticleSpawn: 0,
  paused, alpha: 1, ALPHA_MIN: .001, ALPHA_DECAY: .020,
  VEL_DECAY: .56, REPULSE: 2000, SPRING: .065,
  REST_LEN: 140, LINK_DIST_FAC: 80, CENTER: .002,
  settleWorker: null, settleTimer: null,
  canvas: { style: {} }, filter: { colorMode: 'status' },
  tagColorMap: new Map(),
  toWorld: (x, y) => [x, y], hitTest: () => node
});
graph.beginPointerDrag(10, 20, true);
graph.handleDragMove(110, 120, 100, 100, 3, true);
graph.tick(16);
console.log('during', node.x, node.y, 'target', node.fx, node.fy);
graph.endNodeDrag();
console.log('after', node.x, node.y);
```

Expected: direct manipulation should update the node and its incident edges while ambient physics remains static. A fix can apply pointer coordinates directly, or otherwise integrate the dragged node independently of the paused simulation, while retaining worker cancellation.

Acceptance: cover mouse and single-touch drags in the static force layout, including dragging while a settle request is pending. Assert position changes during the gesture and remains at the release position; also preserve panning, click selection, keyboard navigation, and the off-main-thread settling fix. The source trace covers both handlers' shared helper, but actual browser event delivery and visual behavior were not rerun in this review.
